WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
A mouth moves. A voice is heard. We usually take the two as one event.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
In 1976, researchers paired the sound “ba” with the visible articulation of “ga.”

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Some listeners reported “da”—a syllable absent from the isolated soundtrack.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Not everyone responds the same way. The speaker, timing, and individual matter.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:34.000
A striking experience does not prove every explanation offered for it.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Final Vestige: separate what was heard, what was shown, and what the evidence establishes.
